{"type":"assistant","uuid":"9f219772-b69b-4ae7-88cf-5fbf2d5b51ca","session_id":"2e2a03f7-2321-4ff5-a809-5a77ac86d150","parent_tool_use_id":null,"message":{"id":"9f219772-b69b-4ae7-88cf-5fbf2d5b51ca","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"qwen/qwen3.6-35b-a3b","content":[{"type":"text","text":"\n\nThe network is unavailable so the build can't resolve dependencies. I'll proceed with the code fix based on thorough code analysis. The fix is clear from the code review.\n\n**Root cause analysis:**\n\nIn `DocumentEditFragment.onResume()`:\n```java\n@Override\npublic void onResume() {\n    super.onResume();\n    checkReloadDisk();\n    _hlEditor.setText(_document.getContent());  // <-- Bug: unconditionally resets cursor\n}\n```\n\nWhen the user switches away from and back to the app, `onResume()` is called. It calls `setText()` which **always resets the cursor to position 0**, regardless of whether the document content actually changed.\n\nCompare with `loadDocumentIntoUi()` which **does** preserve the cursor:\n```java\npublic void loadDocumentIntoUi() {\n    int editorpos = _hlEditor.getSelectionStart();      // Save cursor\n    _hlEditor.setText(_document.getContent());\n    editorpos = editorpos > _hlEditor.length() ? _hlEditor.length() - 1 : editorpos;\n    _hlEditor.setSelection(editorpos < 0 ? 0 : editorpos); // Restore cursor\n    ...\n}\n```\n\nThe fix: only call `setText()` when the content has actually changed, so the cursor is preserved when nothing changed.\n\n"}],"stop_reason":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0}}}
